[? if kvp_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#0087DC'> </div> !}KVP: {!</td><td>!} [+ kvp_thuringia_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ kvp_r_thuringia +]%  {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#3E88B3'> </div> !} Traditionalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ traditionalist_thuringia_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ traditionalist_r_thuringia +]%  {!</td></tr>!}

[? if dnf_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#003755'> </div> !}DNF: {!</td><td>!} [+ dnf_thuringia_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ dnf_r_thuringia +]%  {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#7A3C00'> </div> !} Royalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ royalist_thuringia_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ royalist_r_thuringia +]%  {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}
<hr id="read-marker">
Stathmore is currently governed by a broad center-right coalition, which holds exactly half of the state Assembly's seats. This coalition includes all parties to the right of us, along with the special interest parties, the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, both of which have a significant presence in state politics.
<hr id="read-marker">
United Left Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #C43988;">**KPO**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span>?]): [+ left_coalition_thuringia +]% 

Unity Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if unionist_r_thuringia:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> ?][? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]): [+ marcher_coalition_thuringia +]% 

Bourgeois Coalition ([? if unionist_r_thuringia: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>): [+ bourgeois_coalition_thuringia +]%

Right-wing Coalition ([? if unionist_r_thuringia: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>): [+ far_right_coalition_thuringia +]%

[? if royalist_thuringia_elections_vote >= 8: The rapid rise of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in state and local elections is certainly worth keeping an eye on. ?]

@thuringia_coalition_menu
on-arrival: {!
let dvp_toleration_threshold = 50;
let lvp_toleration_threshold = 60;
if (Q.gold_leader == "Eikenvorst") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 5;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Curtius") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology == "Right") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_ideology == "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 15;
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.united_left_thuringia >= 50) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation >= dvp_toleration_threshold && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= lvp_toleration_threshold && Q.lvp_formed)) Q.toleration_possible = 1;
if (((Q.unionist_relation >= 60 || !Q.stegerwald_path) && ((Q.gold_relation >= (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed)))) Q.marcher_coalition_possible = 1;
if ((Q.gold_relation < (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation < (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed)) Q.gold_toleration_threshold_fail = 1;
!}

<hr id="read-marker">
The bourgeois parties have historically been hostile to us in state politics, especially after the notorious <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>-<span style="color: #D47B9B;">**USPD**</span>-<span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> United Left government faced a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> six years ago. They still haven't forgiven the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> for this. 

Meanwhile, the surging <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, now controlling [+ royalist_r_thuringia +]% of the state Assembly, is no longer content with mere toleration and demands a role in government. With the bourgeois parties determined to exclude us from power, Stathmore may well become the first state to appoint a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> minister.

- @toleration_thuringia
- @far_right_coalition_thuringia
- @bourgeois_coalition_thuringia
- @grand_coalition_thuringia
- @united_left_thuringia
- @no_majority
- @spd_majority


@toleration_thuringia
title: The incumbent bourgeois-right government has fallen short of a majority.
subtitle: We will offer our toleration to them, to prevent their dependence on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.
unavailable-subtitle: The bourgeois would rather work with <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> than accept our toleration.
choose-if: toleration_possible
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_thuringia < 50
on-arrival: thuringia_right = 1; pro_republic -= 1; landed_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_other -= 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2

Surprisingly, through our reconciliation with the bourgeois parties, they have accepted our toleration to prevent the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> from entering government. However, this provides valuable propaganda for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, who gain support at the expense of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, who are now tainted by their association with us.

@far_right_coalition_thuringia
title: The incumbent coalition is expanded to include the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.
subtitle: A testament to how biased the "democratic" parties are when it comes to working with us.
view-if: far_right_coalition_thuringia >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition_thuringia < 50
on-arrival: thuringia_royalist = 1; commons_royalist += 2; burgher_royalist += 4; guild_royalist += 6; landed_royalist += 2; disfavored_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_royalist += 2; loyalist_strength += 20; loyalist_militancy += 0.05; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; pro_republic -= 5
face-image: img/portraits/frick.jpg

Wilhelm Frask, a convicted Beer Hall Putsch participant, becomes the first <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> to hold a ministerial-level post in the Commonwealth. He is given control of the Interior and Education Ministries, and by passing an "Enabling Act" through a simple majority as an emergency decree, granting him the power to radically transform Stathmore.

Gone are the days of <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Stathmore. Suspected <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democrats</span> are purged en masse from the civil service. A state police force is established, with Frask preferentially employing <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> officials. All <span style="color: #700000;">communist</span> teachers and mayors are dismissed, and newspapers critical of government policy are banned. [? if heartland_leader == "Bristol" and interior_minister_party == "Marcher": Fortunately, Joshua Heath is able to halt the recruitment of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> into the police force by suspending state subsidies, effectively ending the practice. ?]

With control of the Education Ministry, Frask appoints racial researchers and known <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> to top positions at many universities and bans the anti-war book *All Quiet on the Western Front* from being read or played. His attempts to grant Gallax Commonwealth citizenship have so far failed, forcing Gallax to look elsewhere.

@bourgeois_coalition_thuringia
title: The incumbent center-right coalition continues governing.
subtitle: The incumbent coalition holds a majority, one without the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_thuringia >= 50
on-arrival: thuringia_right = 1; burgher_gold += 2; guild_gold += 2; burgher_other += 2; guild_other += 2; landed_other += 2

Unexpectedly, the parties involved in the incumbent government have gained votes, and now no longer require the votes of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. The continuation of the stable leadership over Stathmore will weaken the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

@grand_coalition_thuringia
title: A [? if lvp_formed: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed: Grand?] Coalition is formed!
subtitle: We have somehow reconciled with the bourgeois parties, that they're willing to govern with us again.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_relation < 60 and stegerwald_path: We need higher relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if gold_toleration_threshold_fail: We need higher relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?]. ?]
view-if: marcher_coalition_thuringia >= 50
choose-if: marcher_coalition_possible
on-arrival: thuringia_marcher = 1; landed_royalist -= 2; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher += 2; landed_marcher += 2; unionist_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; pro_republic += 3; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.03; loyalist_strength -= 25

Somehow, the bourgeois parties are willing to form a [? if lvp_formed: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed: Grand?] Coalition with us, rather than continuing their current government.

We will use our positions in government to root out right-wing and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> sympathies within the civil service and to strengthen <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> sentiment.

@united_left_thuringia
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> will form a coalition government with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
subtitle: History will repeat itself.
view-if: left_coalition_thuringia >= 50 and (collectivist_relation >= 40 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or (collectivist_relation >= 60 and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators")
on-arrival: red_thuringia = 1; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; coup_progress += 3; dufour_angry += 40; vanguard_militancy += 0.05; vanguard_strength += 100; loyalist_strength += 50; warden_strength += 50; strife += 1; commons_marcher += 3; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; landed_marcher -= 3; communist_coalition += 3; collectivist_relation += 10
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/redthuringia.png";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

Surprisingly, despite reluctance on both sides due to fears that the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> DuFour will order a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> if a coalition were to form. <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Stathmore is restored! 

DuFour’s patience is especially thin. Tread carefully.

@spd_majority
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> forms a majority government.
subtitle: Congratulations.
view-if: marcher_r_thuringia >= 50
on-arrival: thuringia_marcher = 1; landed_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 4; guild_royalist -= 4; commons_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_collectivist -= 2; commons_marcher += 2; disfavored_marcher += 2; burgher_marcher += 4; guild_marcher += 4; landed_marcher += 3; pro_republic += 5; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.05; loyalist_strength -= 50

To the sheer horror of the right-wing parties in Stathmore, an unforeseen occurrence has swept over the state: a complete Marchers majority. Members of the far-right cry foul; voter fraud, other forms of subterfuge, and attacks ranging to outright conspiracy is hurled at the results. Nonetheless, <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Stathmore is restored, without the revolutionary concerns of the <span style="color: #D47B9B;">**USPD**</span>/<span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>’s presence in the landtag.

We have undertaken the purging of reactionary sentiments within the police, and revamped the state’s school curriculum to move away from the nationalistic values that remain prevalent. More work is set to be done, but at least DuFour’s gaze has been turned away… for now.

@no_majority
title: No majority can be found!
subtitle: [? if bourgeois_coalition_thuringia < 50 and far_right_coalition_thuringia < 50 and marcher_coalition_thuringia < 50: All possible coalitions lack a majority. ?][? if (bourgeois_coalition_thuringia < 50 and not toleration_possible) or (marcher_coalition_thuringia >= 50 and not marcher_coalition_possible): The bourgeois parties still haven't forgiven us. ?]
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_thuringia < 50 and far_right_coalition_thuringia < 50 and not toleration_possible and not marcher_coalition_possible
on-arrival: {!
let dvp_toleration_threshold = 30;
let lvp_toleration_threshold = 40;
if (Q.gold_leader == "Eikenvorst") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 5;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Curtius") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology == "Right") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_ideology == "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 15;
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.left_coalition_thuringia >= 50) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
}
if (Q.thuringia_no_majority) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold = 0;
    dvp_toleration_threshold = 0;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation >= dvp_toleration_threshold && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= lvp_toleration_threshold && Q.lvp_formed)) Q.toleration_possible = 1;
!}

With the bourgeois parties unable to secure a majority even with the inclusion of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, and their refusal to form a coalition with us, no viable majority can be established. The ruling coalition fears that calling new elections will only accelerate their decline and further erode their support.

In an effort to avoid this, they are more open to negotiating a toleration agreement.

- @toleration_thuringia
- @no_majority_2

@no_majority_2
title: A majority still can't be found!
subtitle: [? if not toleration_possible: This is getting ridiculous. ?][? if toleration_possible: We will refuse to tolerate the bourgeois government, forcing new elections. ?]
on-arrival: thuringia_election_2_trigger_time = time + 3; thuringia_no_majority = 1 if not thuringia_no_majority; thuringia_no_majority += 1 if thuringia_no_majority; burgher_royalist += 4; guild_royalist += 4; landed_royalist += 2; disfavored_royalist += 4; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3 if toleration_possible; guild_marcher -= 3 if toleration_possible; landed_marcher -= 2 if toleration_possible

[? if not toleration_possible: The bourgeois parties remain unwilling to accept our offer of toleration. [? if far_right_coalition_thuringia + ddp_r_thuringia >= 50: One option the incumbent coalition has considered is including both the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, but for obvious reasons, both parties have vetoed this proposal. ?]?][? if toleration_possible: By refusing to enter any toleration agreement, and with the bourgeois parties unwilling to let us lead the government, no majority can be found. As a result, we have shouldered much of the blame for the deadlock and are likely to suffer in the next elections. ?]

With no viable alternatives, the state Assembly faces dissolution, triggering new elections—an opportunity the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> hopes to exploit by capitalizing on political instability and the perceived failure of parliamentary democracy.
